---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import CallButton from '../components/CallButton.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { SITE, lastUpdatedLong } from '../lib/site';
---
<Page
  title="About Baytown Fire and Water Restoration"
  description="Who runs Baytown Fire and Water Restoration, why the site exists, and the editorial standards behind every water and fire damage guide."
  h1="About Baytown Fire and Water Restoration"
  h1Html="About Baytown <em>Fire and Water</em> Restoration"
  eyebrow="About"
  sub="A small local website with one job: help Baytown homeowners understand water and fire damage, and get help by phone, day or night."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap article-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What this site is</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE.brandName} is a help line and guide for homeowners dealing with water, fire and smoke damage in Baytown, Texas. It publishes plain-language guides checked against official sources, and runs a phone line answered 24/7 so you can get a restoration crew scheduled when something goes wrong.
        </p>
        <p>
          Calling is free. If you want to know exactly what happens after you dial, read <a href="/how-it-works/">how calling works, step by step</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Who runs it</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE.brandName} is independently owned and operated. The site owner is responsible for what is published here and reviews each page before it goes live. Questions, corrections and complaints go directly to the owner at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Why it exists</h2>
        <p>
          When a pipe bursts or a kitchen fire is finally out, people search on their phones and call the first number they see. A lot of what they find is not what it claims to be: websites posing as local companies with invented addresses, borrowed reviews and promises nobody intends to keep.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site takes the opposite approach. It tries to earn your trust by being useful: explaining what restoration involves, what Texas rules apply, how insurance usually treats the damage, and how to check the company that shows up.
        </p>

        <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
        <p>Water, fire and mold damage involve your health, your home and your money, so we hold the content to a few firm rules.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Official sources for safety and legal facts.</strong> Health, safety, insurance and licensing statements are based on sources such as the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency, the National Weather Service, the Texas Department of Insurance, the Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation, the U.S. Fire Administration and the American Red Cross. Each page lists its sources.</li>
          <li><strong>No invented numbers.</strong> If we cannot point to a source for a statistic, we do not publish it. We do not quote prices or response times, because we do not set them.</li>
          <li><strong>No fake trust signals.</strong> No made-up reviews, star ratings, awards, certifications, license numbers or addresses. When real reviews exist, we will show real reviews.</li>
          <li><strong>Honest captions.</strong> Every image is captioned for what it shows, and you can see where each one came from in our <a href="/disclaimer/#image-credits">image credits</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Clear limits.</strong> We are not insurance, legal or medical professionals. Pages say so where it matters and point you to people who are.</li>
          <li><strong>Kept current.</strong> Pages are updated when official guidance changes. This page was last updated on {lastUpdatedLong}.</li>
          <li><strong>Corrections welcome.</strong> If you spot an error, email us. We fix confirmed mistakes promptly.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Where we work</h2>
        <p>
          We cover Baytown, Texas only, across ZIP codes {SITE.zips.join(', ')}. Not sure if your street is included? The <a href="/service-area/">Baytown service area map</a> shows the neighborhoods we cover.
        </p>

        <h2>Things you should verify yourself</h2>
        <p>
          Before hiring any restoration company, confirm its insurance, any Texas licenses that apply to your job and its references. Our guide on <a href="/choosing-a-restoration-company-baytown/">how to choose a restoration company</a> walks you through each check, and our <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> explains the limits of our role.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="sidebar" aria-label="Contact">
        <div class="side-box">
          <h2>Need help now?</h2>
          <p>The line is answered 24/7. Call to get a restoration crew scheduled.</p>
          <CallButton label="Call {phone}" location="sidebar" />
        </div>
        <div class="side-box side-box--light">
          <h2>Contact the site owner</h2>
          <p><a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></p>
          <p style="margin:0">Or <a href="/contact/">send us a message</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand heading="Straight answers, <em>local help</em>" text="Call any time, day or night, to talk to a licensed restoration pro, or read the guides first. Either is fine." label="Call {phone}" />
</Page>
